diff --git a/docs/runbooks/partner-outage.md b/docs/runbooks/partner-outage.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/runbooks/partner-outage.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Partner API outage
+
+When the partner reports an outage longer than an hour:
+
+1. Pause the consumer: `cdk deploy PartnerSync-prod -c partnerSyncConsumerEnabled=false`.
+   Updates keep queueing; the queue now holds them for 14 days.
+2. Watch the `partner-sync-backlog-age-prod` alarm; it is expected to fire while paused.
+3. When the partner confirms recovery, resume: `cdk deploy PartnerSync-prod`.
+4. Records the partner still rejects after resuming move to `partner-sync-dlq-prod`
+   after four attempts. Triage them from there with the redrive tool.
+
+Do not purge the queue while paused: the partner has no bulk resync endpoint,
+so the queued updates are the only copy of what changed.

